	<div class="container">
		<div class="embed-wrapper">
			<a href="http://bithub.com/embed?hubId=1&tenant=tropical_leaves_1836_10&view=public" class="bithub-embed">breezy-shelter-3934 Embed</a>
			<div class="embed-overlay"></div>
		</div>
		<p class="embed-caption">BitHub's Bithub</p>
	</div>
</div>
<div class="part">
	<div class="container text-container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-xs-12">
				<h2 class="big-subtitle">Your context, your rules</h2>
				<p>How many times did you see your <b>perfectly crafted post buried under a pile of irrelevant content</b>? But, that's the nature of the social networks. What if you could <b>avoid that problem altogether</b>? What if you could have a place where <b>you control the context</b>? One place where it's everything about you.</p>

				<p>Truth be told, you already have it &dash; it's your own site. With BitHub, you can <b>move the conversation</b> from social networks <b>to your own site</b>, a place where your visitors can became your customers.</p>
				<p>And you know what you can also put on your site? <span class="convert-options"></span>
				</p>
				<blockquote>
					<h3>
						Ninety-two percent of consumers around the world say they trust earned media, such as word-of-mouth and recommendations from friends and family, above all other forms of advertising&hellip;
					</h3>
					<cite>Nielsen Survey 2012.</cite>
				</blockquote>
				<p>Studies show that social proof is one of the most important factors in consumers' decision&dash;making (Nielsen Survey 2012., CompUSA and an iPerceptions study).

				<p>BitHub enables you to gather all your dispersed content in one place and present it as your <b>unified social proof</b>. And the best part? Your content is not mixed with a bunch of other, irellevant posts, tweets and pictures.</p>
				<p>BitHub puts <b>you in control of your brand image</b>, content and context.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="col-xs-12">
				<h2 class="big-subtitle">Features:</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><b>Pull in any content</b> - Twitter, Facebook, Instagram, RSS - all of them are just a click away</li>
					<li><b>Moderate and organize the content</b> - pin posts and block irrelevance</li>
					<li><b>Live Embeds</b> - for any type of event, you can use live version that updates content in near real time</li>
				</ul>
				<div class="emphasized">
					<h2 class="text-center cta">You already spend all this time to produce the right content.<br>Now take the next step and <a href="#registration" class="same-page-link">start converting!</a></h2>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="row">
			<h2 class="col-xs-12 big-subtitle">So, how does it work?</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="features" id="features">
			<div class="feature-left row">
				<div class="image-wrap">
					<img src="/site/images/networks.png" alt="">
				</div>
				<div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6" id="connect">
					<h2>Connect</h2>
					<h3>Aggregate everything!</h3>
					<p>
						BitHub has a powerful aggregation engine which allows you to collect all your content.
					</p>
					<p>
						Twitter, Facebook and Tumblr are just some of the content sources we support. No matter what the content is (text, image or video), we can display it in your feed. All of this works in real time.
					</p>
				</div>


			</div>
			<div class="row">
				<hr class="col-xs-6 col-xs-offset-3 feature-hr">
			</div>
			<div class="feature-right row">
				<div class="image-wrap">
					<img src="/site/images/approve_block.png" alt="">
				</div>
				<div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-offset-6 col-xs-12" id="moderation">
					<h2>Moderate</h2>
					<h3>Your content, your rules.</h3>
					<p>
						Every item we collect is automatically moderated based on the rules you set up. 
					</p>
					<p>
						You can block profanities or filter the data related to some subject. BitHub puts you in control of the data.
					</p>
					<p>
						Besides the automatic moderation, you can manually moderate any item.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row">
				<hr class="col-xs-6 col-xs-offset-3 feature-hr">
			</div>
			<div class="feature-left row">
				<div class="image-wrap">
					<img src="/site/images/design_embed.png" alt="">
				</div>
				<div class="col-sm-6 col-xs-12" id="embed">
					<h2>Embed</h2>
					<h3>Embed on any page.</h3>
					<p>
						BitHub allows you to adjust its design so it fits your branding.
					</p>
					<p>
						All content cards are designed to work in both full page and small area context which allow you to reuse your embeds across your site.
					</p>
					<p>
						Pick your layout and theme, paste the code into your HTML page and you’re ready to go.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="video-wrap">
			<video id="example_video_1" class="video-js vjs-default-skin" controls preload="auto" width="auto" height="auto" data-setup="{}" poster="/site/images/video_poster.png">
				<source src="/site/images/bithub_converted.mp4" type='video/mp4' />
				<source src="/site/images/bithub_converted.webm" type='video/webm' />
				<p class="vjs-no-js">To view this video please enable JavaScript, and consider upgrading to a web browser that <a href="http://videojs.com/html5-video-support/" target="_blank">supports HTML5 video</a></p>
			</video>
		</div>

	</div>
</div>
