	<div class="container text-container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-xs-12">
				<h2 class="big-subtitle">Usage examples</h2>
				<p>BitHub is designed and developed for brands and companies that already have a vibrant community. Some of the ways people use it are:</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-xs-12">
				<div class="usage-lists clearfix">
					<ul>
						<li>Media wall for your event</li>
						<li>Activity stream for your open&dash;source project</li>
						<li>Hashtag contest</li>
						<li>Buzz collector for your festival or concert</li>
					</ul>
					<ul>
						<li>Topic stream for your news portal</li>
						<li>Showcase of your app users</li>
						<li>Community showcase</li>
						<li>Landing page for your app, album or ebook</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				
				
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
<div class="examples-outer-wrapper">
	<div class="container">
		<h3><a href="http://stealjs.com">StealJS</a> is using BitHub to display the activity stream on its homepage</h3>
		<div class="example-embed">
			<a href="http://bithub.com/embed?hubId=1&tenant=charming_volcano_7196_1&view=public" class="bithub-embed">StealJS Embed</a>
			<div class="embed-overlay"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
<div class="part" id="registration">
	<div class="container text-container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-xs-12">
				<h2 class="big-subtitle" id="pricing">Register Your Account</h2>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="frontpage-plan-form clearfix">
			<div class="pricing-registration-page">
				<%= render :partial => 'pricing/per_hub', :locals => {context: 'frontpage'} %>
			</div>
			<div class="registration-panel">
				<%= form_for(Account.new, as: :account, url: registration_path(:account)) do |f| %>

				<div class="plan-and-form-wrap clearfix">

					<div class="panel panel-default">
						<div class="panel-body">


							<div class="form-group"><%= f.label :name %>
								<%= f.text_field :name, autofocus: true, autocomplete: "off", class: 'form-control' %></div>

							<div class="form-group"><%= f.label :email %>
								<%= f.email_field :email, class: 'form-control' %></div>

							<div class="form-group"><%= f.label :password %> <% if @validatable %><i>(<%= @minimum_password_length %> characters minimum)</i><% end %>
								<%= f.password_field :password, autocomplete: "off", class: 'form-control' %></div>

							<div class="form-group"><%= f.label :password_confirmation %>
								<%= f.password_field :password_confirmation, autocomplete: "off", class: 'form-control' %></div>


							<div><%= f.submit "Sign up", class: 'btn btn-primary' %></div>

						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<% end %>

		
	</div>

	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-xs-12">
			<div class="faq-wrap">
				<h2>FAQ</h2>
				<h3>What is a service?</h3>
				<p>A service allows you to load data from a remote source. For instance, you can load a hashtag search from Twitter, RSS URL or a Facebook page updates.</p>
				<h3>How frequent are the stream updates?</h3>
				<p>Most services are crawled and updated either in real time or within 1 minute intervals. Some services (like Twitter followers) are crawled with a maximum delay of 10 minutes.</p>
				<h3>How long does the contract last?</h3>
				<p>After you publish the hub we will charge you on a monthly basis.</p>

				<h3>How do I sign up?</h3>
				<p>By clicking on the link above, you will be able to register for an account. You will be able to test the functionality, and we will start charging you when you're ready to go public with your hub.</p>

				<h3 id="pricing-info">How much will it cost me to use BitHub</h3>
				<p>
					BitHub has a simple unified, pricing. We charge only the public hubs. Public hubs can be embedded on your site. When you publish your hub we will charge you $7 per that hub, per month.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you have two hubs published, we will charge you $7 for each of them - total of $14 per month.
				</p>
				<p>We will charge you at the end of the month, based on how long your hub was published. For instance if you were public for a duration of 3 days, we will charge you only for these 3 days. Minimum charging unit is 1 day.</p>
				<hr>
				<p><b>Do you have any more questions?</b> Feel free to <a href="mailto:mihael@bithub.com">contact us</a>, and we'll get back to you ASAP!</p>
			</div>

		</div>
	</div>
</div>
</div>
